      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "Glucagon-like peptide-1 (GLP-1) is an incretin hormone which has been shown to promote myocardial glucose uptake. Its pharmacological properties as a cardioprotective agent are attractive because it has a short half-life and there is minimal risk of hypoglycaemia."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To assess the hypothesis that intravenous infusion of GLP-1 would protect the heart from ischaemic left ventricular (LV) dysfunction during dobutamine stress echocardiography (DSE) in patients with coronary artery disease (CAD)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "DESIGN",
          "content": "Randomised crossover study."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "PATIENTS AND INTERVENTIONS",
          "content": "14 patients with CAD and good LV function awaiting revascularisation underwent two DSE scans in a randomised order. GLP-1 was infused intravenously at 1.2 pmol/kg/min starting 30 min before the DSE for one of the scans and the other scan acted as a control."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "MAIN OUTCOME MEASUREMENTS",
          "content": "Global and regional wall LV function assessed using tissue Doppler imaging at rest, peak stress and 30 min into recovery."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Global LV function was greater at peak stress during GLP-1 infusion compared with control (ejection fraction 77.0±4.4 vs 70.8±5.0%, p<0.0001; mitral annular systolic velocity 12.18±3.10 vs 11.31±3.11 cm/s, p=0.0004). GLP-1 infusion improved regional wall LV function in 12 non-apical segments assessed by velocity, strain and strain rate. This beneficial effect was predominantly seen in ischaemic segments. In recovery, infusion of GLP-1 mitigated the post-ischaemic stunning seen in the control scan."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Intravenous infusion of GLP-1 protects the heart from ischaemic LV dysfunction induced by dobutamine stress in patients with CAD."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "CLINICAL TRIAL REGISTRATION",
          "content": "URL: http://isrctn.org."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "REGISTRATION NUMBER",
          "content": "ISRCTN 69686930."
        }
      ]},
